  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set for the S3 authentication security audit, prioritized as follows:\n\n1. **`src/rgw/rgw_auth_s3.cc`** / **`.h`** \u2014 core SigV2/SigV4 signature computation and verification (`get_v4_signature`, `get_v2_signature`, canonical request/string-to-sign building, X-Amz-Expires/date parsing)\n2. **`src/rgw/rgw_rest_s3.cc`** / **`.h`** \u2014 S3 REST layer entry point, `RGW_Auth_S3::authorize`, the `AWSEngine`/`AWSGeneralAbstractor` classes that select V2 vs V4 and dispatch to the signature factories\n3. **`src/rgw/rgw_auth.cc`** / **`.h`** \u2014 the generic auth engine/strategy/applier framework RGW's S3 auth plugs into\n4. **`src/rgw/rgw_auth_registry.h`**, **`rgw_auth_filters.h`** \u2014 strategy registry wiring (which engines run and in what order) and auth filter chain\n5. **`src/rgw/rgw_crypt_sanitize.cc`** / **`.h`** \u2014 log redaction for secrets/signatures (relevant to secret-key exposure findings)\n6. **`src/rgw/rgw_acl_types.h`** \u2014 `RGWAccessKey` struct (secret key storage shape)\n7. **`src/rgw/rgw_policy_s3.cc`** / **`.h`** \u2014 browser-upload (POST) policy auth path, a separate signature-verification surface\n8. **`src/rgw/rgw_common.cc`** / **`.h`** \u2014 shared error codes (`SignatureDoesNotMatch`, etc.) and `req_state`\n9. **`src/common/options/rgw.yaml.in`** \u2014 security-relevant config knobs (e.g., presigned-URL deny option, SigV2 support toggle)\n10. **`src/rgw/rgw_rest.cc`** \u2014 REST request dispatch including S3 auth include\n11. **`doc/radosgw/s3/authentication.rst`** \u2014 official documentation of supported auth schemes (V2 deprecated-but-supported, streaming payload signing)\n12. **`src/rgw/driver/rados/rgw_user.h`** \u2014 access-key pool management (secret key access patterns at the storage layer)",
